	<para style="q1"><note caller="-" style="f"><char style="ft">The word <char style="it">God</char>, in place of <char style="it">He who</char>, rests on no sufficient ancient evidence. Some ancient authorities read <char style="it">which</char>.</char></note><char style="w" x-id="t010" x-align="1TI.3.16.a009">He</char> <char style="w" x-id="t011" x-align="1TI.3.16.a009" x-src="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.009" x-source="Ὃς" x-translit="Hos" srcloc="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.009" x-head="true" lemma="ὅς" strong="G3739">who</char> <char style="w" x-id="t012" x-align="1TI.3.16.a010">was</char> <char style="w" x-id="t013" x-align="1TI.3.16.a010" x-src="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.010" x-source="ἐφανερώθη" x-translit="ephanerōthē" srcloc="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.010" x-head="true" lemma="φανερόω" strong="G5319">manifested</char> <char style="w" x-id="t014" x-align="1TI.3.16.a011" x-src="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.011" x-source="ἐν" x-translit="en" srcloc="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.011" x-head="true" lemma="ἐν" strong="G1722">in</char> <char style="w" x-id="t015" x-align="1TI.3.16.a012">the</char> <char style="w" x-id="t016" x-align="1TI.3.16.a012" x-src="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.012" x-source="σαρκί" x-translit="sarki" srcloc="SBLGNT.1TI.3.16.012" x-head="true" lemma="σάρξ" strong="G4561">flesh</char>,</para>
